    "description": "Northwind Fleet Server must support tracing backends supplied by different customers: a local collector for development, an OpenTelemetry exporter for production, and a customer-specific relay added after the server has shipped. The FleetApplication component loads a backend descriptor during start-up, while TelemetryPipeline sends spans through the selected implementation. Backend modules are packaged and versioned separately, and the server must remain usable when one is absent or malformed. Adding a backend must not require changing FleetApplication, recompiling the server, or redeploying it. Configuration may enable exactly one backend per environment and provide credentials, but it must not contain backend behavior. Backend authors need to document the descriptor contract, provide a compatibility version, and test their module independently. The server should reject unknown descriptor versions, log discovery failures without crashing, and keep the local collector available as an operator fallback. The decision is whether the server should obtain tracing behavior from independently packaged, discoverable modules or keep each possible backend inside the server source tree.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide whether Fleet Server should acquire tracing backends from separately packaged modules discovered at start-up, rather than compiling every backend into the server.",
    "notes": "Plugin fits tracing backends shipped as separately packaged modules discovered at start-up; factory-kit is the near-miss (caller-registered builders) and envelope-letter supports the stable facade over swappable implementations. Removed traits from supporting: compile-time type descriptors do not fit this run-time discovery design."
  },
